Starting today, Apple is making its U.S. website available in Spanish. Customers who have Spanish set as their language will be able to browse apple.com/us-es by default, and anyone will be able to choose Spanish from the country and language selector at the bottom of the website.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/apple-spanish.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1077678" /><br/>
While most of the site will be available in Spanish, the Apple Online Store and Financial Services will be in English only. Customers who visit the Apple Online Store can shop in Spanish by contacting an Apple Specialist by phone.<br/>
<br/>
